Obrii LoRaWAN module

Independent C++17 LoRaWAN 1.0.4 / 1.1 protocol implementation, EU868 Class A/B/C
helpers and LoRa IQ adapter. The core opens no GUI, hardware or sockets.
The mesh constructor uses a separate host adapter.
Specifications: LoRa Alliance TS001-1.0.4, LoRaWAN 1.1 (including the FOpts
encryption counter-domain erratum), and EU863-870 regional parameters.
This is not a certified LoRaWAN stack or a claim of full MAC compliance.

AES block primitive uses the unmodified tiny-AES-c files already present in
third_party/tiny_aes (revision 23856752fbd139da0b8ca6e471a13d5bcc99a08d),
under the Unlicense. See installed unlicense.txt. Obrii implements CMAC,
LoRaWAN packet construction and state management around the block primitive.
When linking the IQ adapter, also retain src/lora/NOTICE and LICENSE.LoRaPHY.

Independent protocol vectors reference the MIT-licensed brocaar/lorawan library:
https://github.com/brocaar/lorawan/tree/4bb09b3bdacba097680894e8d35dbcbc0d260c7e
Its implementation is only a test dependency in the ignored build/ directory;
it is not linked into the production C++ library.
